    [Doc][Misc] Correct and extend Qwen3.5-397B-A17B deployment guide (#18233)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Align the model guide with the author's updated deployment
    configurations, and resolve conflicts with the latest target branch's
    memory-unit cleanup.
    
    - Replace A3 PD with a single-host, 16-NPU W4A8 example: Prefill uses
    devices 0–7 with TP8/DP1; Decode uses devices 8–15 with TP4/DP2.
    Document the shared service IP and separate service/transfer ports.
    - Replace 950DT PD with a two-host W4A8C8/MXFP8 example using Prefill
    TP8/DP1 and Decode TP4/DP2, `MooncakeConnectorV2`, and the corresponding
    C8 requirements.
    - Include complete proxy commands beside each A3, 950DT, and A2
    deployment. Keep the A3/A2 V1 and 950DT V2 connectors paired with the
    standard Pull proxy, and keep MTP method/token count consistent on P and
    D.
    - Use MC2 mode `1` for the single-node examples, mode `2` for the
    supplied A3 PD configuration, and mode `0` for 950DT W4A8C8 PD. Retain
    the A2 positional interface and its hardware-specific settings.
    - Update topology/parameter tables, Function Calling, evaluation
    examples, tuning guidance, and FAQs. Keep `Atlas 800I A2`/`Atlas 800I
    A3` naming and explicit GB units.
    - Add `Text, image, video` to the two Qwen397B multimodal Note cells in
    the support matrix. Keep the Qwen397B entries identical across both PRs,
    including the author's A2/A3 supported status.
    
    - Use `Eco-Tech/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-w4a8c8-mxfp` in the model-weight table
    and 950DT PD introduction, and link its MXFP8 KV cache setting to
    Section 5.5. Keep the model guide byte-identical between both PRs.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation and reference deployment commands only; no runtime source
    code or API changes relative to the target branch.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Markdownlint 0.45.0 passed for the model guide and support matrix; the
    PR diff against the updated target branch passes `git diff --check`.
    - All 25 Shell/Bash blocks passed syntax checks; both Python snippets
    and all 39 quoted JSON values parsed.
    - Verified 31 unique local file/section links, including cross-document
    anchors after expanding includes.
    - Checked 10 deployment commands against nine configuration-table rows
    and all three P/D/proxy groups. Verified MTP, KV topology/roles/dtype,
    recompute scope, A3 device separation, and service ports.
    - Both model-guide versions are identical. Conflict resolution preserves
    the author's supplied document, with only upstream whitespace cleanup
    applied.
    - Rebuilt the documentation changes as linear history on the latest
    target branch, eliminating the intermediate revisions that conflicted
    during CI rebase. The PR changes only the model guide and support
    matrix.
    - Re-ran the CI-equivalent `git rebase` against the target branch
    successfully; Markdownlint and `git diff --check` passed after
    rebuilding the history.
    - Required `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but could not complete
    because `pre-commit` is not installed locally.
    - No new NPU deployment, accuracy, or performance run was performed;
    runtime and performance validation remains specific to the selected
    hardware/software/checkpoint stack.
    
